  {
    "gold": "49",
    "question": "For the summer, the clothing store has a 50% discount for all items. On Wednesdays, there is an additional $10.00 off on all jeans after the summer discount is applied.  Before the sales tax applies, the cost of a pair of jeans is $14.50. How much was the original cost for the jeans before all the discounts?",
    "question_sha256": "c6bd517fd7c7cbf92c245c20bea41ea0e764e67b0c6a38924eb1da0d8b4b5d44",
    "responses": [
      {
        "key": "gsm8k-train-3079:rich",
        "raw_call_sha256": "ce39f257f7f1e5aecfd0803bc43b2151da5ee75d2a8f45fba15118cf007c37d8",
        "student_prefix": [
          {
            "content": "For the summer, the clothing store has a 50% discount for all items. On Wednesdays, there is an additional $10.00 off on all jeans after the summer discount is applied.  Before the sales tax applies, the cost of a pair of jeans is $14.50. How much was the original cost for the jeans before all the discounts?",
            "role": "user"
          }
        ],
        "student_prefix_sha256": "bc6882c2fe9bf31d3417ae959f924adad4d3b9da647dd6e5533130be1a9054a7",
        "target": "Given:\n- The final cost of jeans after all discounts is $14.50.\n- There is an additional $10.00 off on Wednesdays after the 50% summer discount is applied.\n\nFirst, let's reverse the $10.00 off to find the cost before this discount:\n\\[ \\text{Cost before Wednesday discount} = \\$14.50 + \\$10.00 = \\$24.50 \\]\n\nNext, we reverse the 50% summer discount. A 50% discount means the customer pays 50% of the original price. So, the $24.50 represents 50% of the original price:\n\\[ \\text{Original price} = \\frac{\\$24.50}{0.50} = \\$49.00 \\]\n\nThus, the original cost of the jeans before all the discounts was $49.00.\n\nFINAL: 49",
        "target_sha256": "db88f5272eabffdf7a9af253c2f39643c6860e63afa243bea95d6ad7cc00d6c6"
      },
      {
        "key": "gsm8k-train-3079:new_record",
        "raw_call_sha256": "3b5b94e2a9597b87d15151a92c751928187fefc6553674a6ce3bcc211d9018f3",
        "student_prefix": [
          {
            "content": "For the summer, the clothing store has a 50% discount for all items. On Wednesdays, there is an additional $10.00 off on all jeans after the summer discount is applied.  Before the sales tax applies, the cost of a pair of jeans is $14.50. How much was the original cost for the jeans before all the discounts?",
            "role": "user"
          },
          {
            "content": "Given:\n- The final cost of jeans after all discounts is $14.50.\n- There is an additional $10.00 off on Wednesdays after the 50% summer discount is applied.\n\nFirst, let's reverse the $10.00 off to find the cost before this discount:\n\\[ \\text{Cost before Wednesday discount} = \\$14.50 + \\$10.00 = \\$24.50 \\]\n\nNext, we reverse the 50% summer discount. A 50% discount means the customer pays 50% of the original price. So, the $24.50 represents 50% of the original price:\n\\[ \\text{Original price} = \\frac{\\$24.50}{0.50} = \\$49.00 \\]\n\nThus, the original cost of the jeans before all the discounts was $49.00.\n\nFINAL: 49",
            "role": "assistant"
          },
          {
            "content": "Write your own reusable record of this solved task.",
            "role": "user"
          }
        ],
        "student_prefix_sha256": "09278774f06673e536b972427c046e2ffc3344894ece81e8f821fe80708bab9b",
        "target": "Given the problem, I identified the following quantities and the unknown:\n- The final cost of jeans after all discounts is $14.50.\n- There is an additional $10.00 off on Wednesdays after the 50% summer discount is applied.\n- The unknown is the original cost of the jeans before all the discounts.\n\nTo solve this, I first needed to reverse the $10.00 off discount. This means adding $10.00 to the final cost to find the price before the Wednesday discount:\n\\[ \\text{Cost before Wednesday discount} = \\$14.50 + \\$10.00 = \\$24.50 \\]\n\nNext, I needed to reverse the 50% summer discount. A 50% discount means the customer pays 50% of the original price, so the $24.50 represents 50% of the original price. To find the original price, I divided $24.50 by 0.50:\n\\[ \\text{Original price} = \\frac{\\$24.50}{0.50} = \\$49.00 \\]\n\nTo check the result, I would apply the discounts in reverse order:\n1. Start with the original price of $49.00.\n2. Apply the 50% summer discount: \\( \\$49.00 \\times 0.50 = \\$24.50 \\).\n3. Apply the $10.00 off Wednesday discount: \\( \\$24.50 - \\$10.00 = \\$14.50 \\).\n\nThe final cost matches the given final cost, confirming the solution is correct.\n\nFINAL: 49",
        "target_sha256": "ebdf8a8044c3882ba1283de7f8e10165162661f229f35fddaf9adb1f20fe94ec"
