        "student_prefix": [
          {
            "content": "A group of parents get together and decide to hire a private school teacher to quit his job and teach their children.  His former job paid 45,000 per year and they offered him a 20% raise.  If there are 9 kids how much does each parent have to pay?",
            "role": "user"
          }
        ],
        "student_prefix_sha256": "1ef43d0feb8d8b387c577a66126ac5aecbd0ae86435b83ea669cb072972d2251",
        "target": "The private school teacher's former salary was $45,000 per year. They offered him a 20% raise, so the new salary is calculated as follows:\n\n1. Calculate the raise amount: \\( 45,000 \\times 0.20 = 9,000 \\)\n2. Add the raise to the original salary: \\( 45,000 + 9,000 = 54,000 \\)\n\nSo, the new salary is $54,000. There are 9 kids, and the total cost is to be divided among the parents. Therefore, each parent has to pay:\n\n\\[ \\frac{54,000}{9} = 6,000 \\]\n\nEach parent has to pay $6,000.\n\nFINAL: 6000",
        "target_sha256": "478180cf1eb9049c92a403bb2fd903d4347972c58c65d78f1b79c44265d35907"
