          },
          {
            "content": "The private school teacher's former salary was $45,000 per year. They offered him a 20% raise, so the new salary is calculated as follows:\n\n1. Calculate the raise amount: \\( 45,000 \\times 0.20 = 9,000 \\)\n2. Add the raise to the original salary: \\( 45,000 + 9,000 = 54,000 \\)\n\nSo, the new salary is $54,000. There are 9 kids, and the total cost is to be divided among the parents. Therefore, each parent has to pay:\n\n\\[ \\frac{54,000}{9} = 6,000 \\]\n\nEach parent has to pay $6,000.\n\nFINAL: 6000",
            "role": "assistant"
          },
          {
            "content": "Write your own reusable record of this solved task.",
            "role": "user"
          }
        ],
        "student_prefix_sha256": "78d9b6a984b21e5721bb48f200b4f797852e772fdb40d746473380e14d005456",
        "target": "Given the problem, I identified the following quantities:\n- The teacher's former salary: $45,000 per year\n- The raise percentage: 20%\n- The number of children: 9\n\nThe unknown quantity is the amount each parent has to pay.\n\nTo find the new salary, I first calculated the raise amount:\n\\[ 45,000 \\times 0.20 = 9,000 \\]\n\nThen, I added the raise to the original salary:\n\\[ 45,000 + 9,000 = 54,000 \\]\n\nNext, I divided the new salary by the number of children to find out how much each parent has to pay:\n\\[ \\frac{54,000}{9} = 6,000 \\]\n\nTo check the result, I multiplied the amount each parent has to pay by the number of children to ensure it equals the new salary:\n\\[ 6,000 \\times 9 = 54,000 \\]\n\nThis confirms that the calculation is correct. The operation I would reuse is dividing the total cost by the number of children to find the individual contribution, as it directly addresses the unknown quantity based on the given facts.\n\nFINAL: 6000",
